{
  "about": [
    "F1 checklist-matrix oracle, WRITTEN BY HAND from the loader's design rules (facility layers identified by file name; manifest layers shown as found; tier columns). Not generated from the code.",
    "Inputs: the synthetic bundles written by tests/synthetic/make_bundles.js under local-test-artifacts/f1/ ('source' is relative to that folder; tiers are checked both as ZIP and as folder). Also: the landing page's downloadable sample (sample/CVI_sample_bundle_synthetic.zip, the Full tier's files in one folder) must give exactly the Full expectations.",
    "datasets: dataset id -> the file name used, 'missing', or {\"conflict\": [file names]}. Datasets not listed must be 'missing'.",
    "files: every file the loader passes on -> 'used:<dataset>', 'bundle', 'conflict:<dataset>' or 'not-used:<fragment of the reason>'. The list is complete.",
    "via: how a used file was recognized ('columns', 'name', 'name column', 'bundle.json'), for the files listed.",
    "missingUseful: dataset id -> first column of each optional column group that is absent (feature switches and later-version notes).",
    "features: feature id -> 'on' or 'off:<fragment of the reason>' (feature gating, checklist.js).",
    "options: 'choices' is the user's pick for a conflict (dataset -> file name); 'assign' is the user's pick in the 'which layer is this file?' picker (file name -> dataset). The test harness turns file names into the loader's file ids; names are unique within each case. (Every bundle.json case has a real bundle.json, read by bundle.js.)",
    "bundle: the banner text shown from bundle.json (null = no banner) and fragments of the warnings expected (an empty list = no warnings). Cases without 'bundle' expect no banner and no warnings.",
    "candidates: file name -> the dataset ids the picker offers for an unclear file, in dataset-list order.",
    "fileWarnings: file name -> fragment of the warning shown on that file (e.g. a bundle.json entry that does not fit; since audit D3-04 such an entry no longer stops the file being recognized by its columns). Files not listed have no warning.",
    "layers: file name -> the facility layer ids the file could be (columns fit; narrowed to layers whose own name column it has, when any), in dataset-list order. The page offers its 'change layer' dropdown when there is more than one.",
    "Audit E-01 (F1-R9): master_extra_columns and master_named_like_facility: a file with every master column is the master even with a facility layer's extra columns (name, lat, long) or a facility layer's recommended name; it gets no change-layer dropdown.",
    "S2a day 2 (2026-10-05): features 'summaries' and 'spotlight' need the master table only (as 'wa-map'); 'unique-cvis' also needs the CVI column, which only the Full tier's master has among these inputs.",
    "S2b (2026-10-06): feature 'period-modes' (Browse over time and Compare two periods) needs the master table only, so it is on or off with 'spotlight' in every scenario (added by that rule).",
    "S4 (2026-10-07): feature 'flow-map' (National Flow map) needs the master table only (its state files are bundled), so it is on or off with 'period-modes' in every scenario (added by that rule)."
  ],
